      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Cloud Vision AI**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Vision AI. The next step is to make this choice explicit in the Python script itself. I'll need to install the appropriate client libraries and structure the code so it's readily apparent which external service I'm leveraging.\n\n\n**Implementing the Choice**\n\nNow I am creating the `detect_image_labels.py` file and writing the Python code. I'm focusing on making the Google Cloud Vision AI integration explicit. This includes the required imports, client initialization, and an easily identifiable placeholder for the image path.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863111163,
          "start": 1789863109056
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc27a1c000146VkaiX6cnGyEF",
